  "schema": "nfl2k5_board_kit/v1",
  "sources": [
    "Sports Video Group, 'Heinz Field, Pittsburgh Steelers Continue Partnership With Daktronics' (2014-04-29, https://www.sportsvideo.org/2014/04/29/heinz-field-pittsburg-steelers-continue-partnership-with-daktronics/): a display about 35 ft high by 72 ft wide (13HD) in the northwest end zone, supplementing the south board. StadiumsOfProFootball.com: a 35 x 73 ft HD scoreboard installed in the northwest corner before the 2014 season, and the 28 x 96 ft video board (Daktronics HD, 2007) over the open south end.",
    "The retail s22 scene (PROVED OFFLINE): +z is the open south end, whose screen (digits2, 28.5 x 8.6 m, y 20.6 to 29.2) is already the 2007 board's size within 3 % (96 x 28 ft = 29.3 x 8.5 m), so it stays; u4's 2026 venue art renames its surround (ad_bb01) and takes its defunct sponsors off. The northwest corner is an open notch between the west upper deck's north end (x -77.9 to -57.3 at z -74.8 to -66.6) and the north stands' west end (x -50.0 to -43.2 at z -111.6 to -90.0), over the corner's floor at y 10.4 to 11.3.",
    "The Heinz ketchup bottles came off the scoreboard when the stadium was renamed in July 2022 (TribLIVE, 'Heinz ketchup bottles removed from scoreboard at Acrisure Stadium'; CBS Pittsburgh, 'Ketchup bottles come down from newly named Acrisure Stadium'); one returned in 2023 outside the Heinz Gate, not on the board. The retail scene (PROVED OFFLINE) lays them on top of the south scoreboard (x +-9.1 to +-22.6, y 35.4 to 38.8, z 89.8, with the pouring drips at z 89.9; in the night and afternoon bundles in temp_bottle_group19); the kit cuts them.",
    "Commons, 'Ptr-HeinzField-FILE.jpg' (2020 aerial from the north, r014): the board seen from behind in the north end's west part, a steel-framed box standing on two posts on the concourse deck, well west of the goalposts (reference only; no pose solved).",
    "DESIGN (no inside photo of it): the board spans the northwest notch between the two stands' ends, square to the field centre (centre x -52.3, z -82.1), its top level with the stands' rims (32.0 m), on two 0.6 m steel posts down to the corner's floor, as the aerial shows; frame, body and posts in the retail roof and pole materials at a steel grey.",
    "DESIGN (main, 2026-09-29): the boards' bodies and backs take bb_color, a plain retail material, at their dark colour (a solid panel from behind); the frame's material stays on the thin border only."
  ],
